---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import { LEGAL } from "../config/site";
const crumbs = [{ name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy/" }];
---
<Base title="Reelbird privacy: no account needed, no telemetry" description="Recordings stay on your Mac. No analytics, no crash reporting, no update checks. Shares go to the bucket you configure, or to Reelbird Pro if you choose it." og="privacy" crumbs={crumbs}>
  <PageHead title="Privacy" lede="Reelbird needs no account. Your recordings stay on your Mac unless you share them, and then they go to storage you own, or to Reelbird Pro's hosting if you choose it." crumbs={crumbs} />
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose body">
      <p>This policy covers the Reelbird app, Reelbird Pro (watch.reelbird.app) and this website. {LEGAL.operator} runs Reelbird Pro and this website and is responsible for the personal data described here. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="app">The app</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Recordings, edits, captions and transcripts stay on your Mac, in <code>~/Movies/Reelbird</code> unless you choose another folder.</li>
        <li>Find Sensitive Info reads the text on screen with Apple's on-device text recognition to suggest blurs. Nothing is uploaded, and the command line and MCP server show only masked previews of what it finds. It reads the screen only, not narration, captions or overlays such as keystrokes.</li>
        <li>Captions and titles are made on your Mac by Apple's frameworks. No API keys and no cloud services. On macOS 26, macOS downloads Apple's speech model the first time you make captions.</li>
        <li>Nothing is uploaded unless you share. With your own bucket, shares go only there, signed with your own keys. The secret key lives in your macOS Keychain and is only sent to your storage endpoint as a request signature.</li>
        <li>No analytics, no telemetry, no crash reporting and no update checks. The app only contacts the Reelbird server if you sign in to Reelbird Pro.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="links">Share links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Links are unlisted, not secret.</strong> Anyone who has a link can watch the video, download it and forward the link. Random IDs make links impossible to guess, and the storage isn't listable, but there's no password.</li>
        <li><strong>Sharing while recording uploads as you go.</strong> If you discard the take, Reelbird deletes everything it uploaded for it. That quick version has no edits. When you update the link with your edits (blurs included), Reelbird replaces the quick version and deletes its files, along with captions or posters you removed.</li>
        <li><strong>Stop sharing</strong> deletes every file for that link. A CDN cache may serve a deleted file for a short time, and anyone who downloaded the video keeps their copy.</li>
        <li><strong>What viewers load.</strong> With your own bucket, the viewer page, video and captions all come from your bucket. While a share has only the live stream, browsers without built-in HLS (Chrome, Firefox) also load the hls.js player from jsDelivr, pinned to one version and integrity-checked. Once you update the link, viewers get a plain MP4 and nothing else. With Reelbird Pro, the page comes from <code>watch.reelbird.app</code> and also loads a small script that counts views (below).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>More in <a href="/docs/sharing/#privacy">Sharing setup → Privacy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="pro">Reelbird Pro (optional)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your account</strong> is your email address. We use it to sign you in and to send messages about your account and billing, nothing else: no newsletters and no ads. Signing in from the app gives it a token stored in your macOS Keychain; we keep only a hash of it.</li>
        <li><strong>Your shared videos</strong> are stored in Reelbird's private Cloudflare R2 bucket, under the link's random ID, with the title you gave them. Viewers get short-lived signed links to the files. Deleting a link deletes its files and its view records.</li>
        <li><strong>Viewer analytics are anonymous and use no cookies.</strong> A view counts once someone has played at least 3 seconds. For each view we record how much of the video was played, the referring site, the device type and browser, and the country when known. Unique viewers come from a hash of IP address, browser and link that changes every day, so no IP address is stored, nobody can be followed across days or links, and one person watching on three days counts three times. You never see who a viewer is. Your own plays while signed in, and link-preview bots, aren't counted. Only you see your links' numbers.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments</strong> are handled by Stripe; we never see your card number. We keep your Stripe customer ID, email and subscription status to know your plan.</li>
        <li><strong>Reports.</strong> If you report a link, we keep your email and report to handle it.</li>
        <li>Cancel any time from your <a href="https://watch.reelbird.app/account">account page</a> (<strong>Manage billing</strong>). Your links keep playing after Pro ends; delete them from the account page or the app.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="processors">Who processes Reelbird Pro data</h2>
      <p>We use these providers only to run the service, under their data processing terms:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hetzner</strong> (servers in Germany): runs watch.reelbird.app and its database.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: R2 storage for hosted videos.</li>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong>: subscriptions and payments.</li>
        <li><strong>Twilio SendGrid</strong>: delivers sign-in emails.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some of them are in the United States, so your data may be processed there. We don't sell or rent personal data, and we don't share it with advertisers.</p>

      <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Account and billing records: while you have an account, and billing records afterwards for as long as tax and accounting law requires.</li>
        <li>Hosted videos and their view records: until you delete the link or your account.</li>
        <li>Sign-in links expire after 15 minutes and are deleted within a day. Signed-out and expired sessions are deleted.</li>
        <li>Server request logs: kept briefly to run and secure the service, then deleted.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>You can delete links yourself from your account page or the app. To get a copy of your data, correct it, or delete your account and everything in it, email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a> from your account's address. Depending on where you live (for example the EU, UK or California), you may have further rights, including to object or complain to a data protection authority. We'll answer within 30 days. Reelbird Pro isn't meant for children under 13.</p>

      <h2 id="site">This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies and no advertising or cross-site trackers. Fonts, images and the product clips are served from this site.</li>
        <li>The launch film on the home page is hosted on YouTube. Nothing loads from YouTube until you press play; then the video loads from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> and Google's privacy policy applies to it.</li>
        <li>We count visits with <a href="https://umami.is">Umami</a>, which we host ourselves. It sets no cookies, stores no IP addresses and records only the page, referrer, browser, device type and country. It never runs inside the Reelbird app.</li>
        <li>Your theme choice, if you pick one, is kept in your browser's local storage and never sent anywhere.</li>
        <li>The server that hosts this site may keep standard request logs (such as IP address, page and time) to keep it running.</li>
        <li>Donations on the Support page and the Pro checkout go to Stripe, where Stripe's privacy policy applies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy in a way that matters, we'll update the date below and email Reelbird Pro customers before it takes effect.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>. For bugs, open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/btahir/reelbird/issues">GitHub</a>. For a security problem, follow the repository's <a href="https://github.com/btahir/reelbird/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security policy</a>.</p>
      <p class="muted">Last updated {LEGAL.updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .body { padding-bottom: var(--section); }
</style>
